{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>And Elohim blessed them.</b> And likewise: ״ויברך אלהים את יום השביעי״. Thus you learn that one who acquires a new thing recites the blessing shehecheyanu." "<b>Be fruitful and multiply.</b> But mules were not included in the blessing, as we say: ״הוא ענה, אשר מצא את הימים במדבר״ — and therefore they are not fruitful and do not multiply in the world. And even according to Rabbi Yose, who concludes in the chapter מקום שנהגו that at the close of the Sabbath of creation Adam brought two animals and mated one upon the other and a mule came out of them — there is no difficulty at all, for 'be fruitful and multiply' was said before." "<b>And subdue it.</b> Defective [in] vav, to teach you that it is the way of the man to subdue the female, so that she not be given to promiscuity, to cause stumbling to licentiousness, as Leah did — she accustomed [her daughter], and caused a stumbling to her daughter. And any woman who keeps herself modest inside the house is fit to marry a High Priest, as it is said: ״כל כבודה בת מלך פנימה״ etc. — that is, she should marry one about whom it is written ושבצת. And she is fit to raise from [herself] High Priests, as it is said: ״בניך כשתילי זיתים״, who are anointed with olive oil."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T23:15:54.776313092Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}